1
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,080
Turn on the lights and take a step back,
will you?

2
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:42,640
We'll manage somehow, I'm sure.

3
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:47,900
You understand, right?
Yeah, yeah, I understand.

4
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:51,800
Once you get it, keep quiet and follow me.

5
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:10,300
Whaaaaaat?

6
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,420
Well then, I'm counting on you again, okay?

7
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:42,600
Whoa! Oof!

8
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:43,900
Hey!

9
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:46,080
Hey!

10
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:49,400
Mm... mm... mm...

11
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:49,680
Mm...

12
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:53,880
Are you okay?

13
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:55,780
Wa... water...

14
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,260
Have you calmed down?

15
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:09,100
Where am I?

16
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,300
It's Hakodate, though.

17
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:11,960
Hakodate.

18
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:14,600
Excuse me, but

19
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,920
Who am I?

20
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:20,680
Who on earth am I...

21
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,400
Who am I, anyway?

22
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:26,220
Dammit, who am I?

23
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:37,140
You don't even know who you are?!
And I can't remember at all why I'm here.

24
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:42,300
Amnesia I've never seen
your face around this town.

25
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,300
Why do I call myself "washi"?

26
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:51,260
Should I contact the police for now?

27
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:53,300
Police? What's wrong?

28
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:59,000
No, hearing
"police" makes me feel oddly nostalgic, yet somehow uneasy.

29
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:04,240
Got it, got it.
Then let's forget about the police.

30
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:05,840
Really?

31
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:06,420
Yeah.

32
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:11,880
Then do you have anything on
you that shows who you are?

33
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:16,380
Why do you only have stuff like this?

34
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:17,320
Yeah.

35
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,960
You don't have anything else?

36
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:32,720
How about it?

37
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:35,840
Nothing at all.

38
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,300
I see, so no leads.

39
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:39,160
Yeah.

40
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:44,440
So, what are you going to do now?

41
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,060
I don't know what to do.

42
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:50,120
Why don't you come to my place for now?

43
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:52,020
Is that really okay?

44
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:54,600
Yeah, I'm Kano Ryoji.

45
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:56,520
My place is right nearby.

46
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:01,280
Thanks, you really saved me.

47
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,520
Hey, Ryo-san.

48
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:03,920
What is it?

49
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:06,460
Aya-chan said not to make any detours,

50
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:08,660
and to hurry back home.

51
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:09,980
Got it?

52
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,220
Got it.

53
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:13,180
See you.

54
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:16,220
You just answered to that, didn't you?

55
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:18,260
I guess I just did it without thinking.

56
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:22,000
Maybe people used to call you Ryo-san too?

57
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:23,640
Maybe so.

58
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:26,420
Then what's your name?
Something like Ryosuke, maybe?

59
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,160
I don't think that's it.

60
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:33,880
Then how about Ryohei, Ryozo, or Ryota?

61
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,720
None of them ring a bell.

62
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,800
I see.

63
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:39,280
Well, no need to rush.

64
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:41,620
Take your time and remember slowly.

65
00:04:49,940 --> 00:04:52,500
But with that outfit,
the house would be the one who's surprised

66
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:55,280
Why are you hesitating to say it?

67
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:57,600
Well, I don't even know myself.

68
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:59,080
Is that really okay?

69
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,040
This is what feels most natural to me.

70
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:06,940
Amnesia?

71
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:11,120
I was thinking you could
stay at my place for a while.

72
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:12,640
Nice to meet you. Please take care of me.

73
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:13,880
You there.

74
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:14,060
How about it?

75
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,820
Yeah, I don't see why not.

76
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:23,540
Bro, the radio cassette stopped working.

77
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:27,460
What's this kid doing?
And we've got a customer here.

78
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:29,380
Welcome.

79
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:31,620
This is my little sister, Aya.

80
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:32,740
Hello.

81
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:35,080
Bro, the radio cassette.

82
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:38,020
Don't tell me. Tell Dad.

83
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,960
Mind if I take a look at that?

84
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:51,420
Bro, that guy's an electrician.

85
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:52,420
Well...

86
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:55,780
Yes.

87
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,300
Covered by a high-pressure system.

88
00:05:59,300 --> 00:05:59,960
Thank you.

89
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,600
Here you go.

90
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,920
Thanks.

91
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:13,220
You really can't remember anything?

92
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:16,280
Not even your name. Nothing at all.

93
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:19,560
But you're sure you were
called Ryo-san, right?

94
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,640
Probably.

95
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:25,560
What's gotten into this kid,
suddenly being so nice?

96
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:29,720
Just because he fixed her radio cassette,
she's so fickle.

97
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:34,340
Hmph. Well,
he's nothing like you, big brother.

98
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,340
But how did he manage to fix it?

99
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:40,760
Maybe he really is an electrician after all.

100
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:45,980
Well, I don't know myself,
but my hands just moved on their own.

101
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,100
Ryotsu's not in today either?

102
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,820
Yes, it seems he hasn't
gone back to the dorm either.

103
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:00,220
Skipping work is nothing new for him,

104
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:02,800
but for him to be completely
unreachable like this...

105
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,860
What an outrageous fellow.

106
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:06,700
In that case, I'll consult with the chief

107
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:09,040
and have him fired for dereliction of duty.

108
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:12,100
But I wonder what on
earth has happened to him.

109
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:14,480
I hope nothing has happened.

110
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:16,440
He should just be left alone.

111
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,520
Wherever that guy ends up,
whatever happens to him,

112
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:19,600
it's none of my business.

113
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:25,820
Well, see you around.

114
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:26,620
Yeah.

115
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,420
Sorry to keep you waiting, Ryo-san.

116
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:31,320
Yeah.

117
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:33,220
Well, shall we head home?

118
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:35,960
Sorry. I keep relying on you.

119
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:37,340
Don't worry about it.

120
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:40,860
If you want,
I can at least lend you a hand, Ryo.

121
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:42,580
I appreciate the thought, though.

122
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,320
I'm not really in a position

123
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:48,660
to help, since I'm in such a sorry
state that I'm working on my buddy's boat.

124
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:50,620
You don't have a boat of your own?

125
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,460
I do have one, but...

126
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:55,580
It's in pretty bad shape.

127
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:01,720
It's been in use since my old man's day.

128
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:05,720
Even if I wanted a new one,
I've got no savings at all.

129
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:17,480
Could you lend me some tools?

130
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:19,300
Right.

131
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:24,060
You can fix boats too?

132
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:25,720
I don't know.

133
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:29,460
I don't know,
but I've got a feeling I can do it.

134
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:29,760
Yeah.

135
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:34,280
Maybe you were a carpenter or something?

136
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:40,720
Well, I feel like I usually
make much smaller things.

137
00:08:57,540 --> 00:08:58,460
You're amazing.

138
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:00,180
Fixing even a boat!

139
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:03,480
From now on, let me call you big brother.

140
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:06,720
Please, big brother.

141
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,320
It's kind of embarrassing

142
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:09,940
Come on, what's the harm?

143
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:11,480
Hey, big brother!

144
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:12,580
Number one in Japan!

145
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,180
Your father would be
happy to see this, I bet.

146
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:54,340
Doesn't your father
still go out on the boat?

147
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,540
Not since he hurt his back.

148
00:09:57,740 --> 00:09:59,840
Now he works at the pachinko
parlor in front of the station.

149
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:02,560
But deep down,
he still wants to be out on the boat.

150
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:04,660
Ryo-san.

151
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:07,220
How did it go today?

152
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:09,700
A huge haul!

153
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:14,760
A huge haul

154
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,660
All thanks to you, big brother.

155
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:20,360
Right.

156
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,860
No, no, not like that.

157
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:23,920
Let's go with this one. This one.

158
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,900
Well then.

159
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:29,240
Come on, good, good.

160
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,360
Yes, thank you. I'll have some.

161
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:36,860
Look at him drink!

162
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:39,360
Come on, let's take this over.

163
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,540
Dad.

164
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:42,700
Your old man's happy too.

165
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:44,640
Shut up, Ryoji.

166
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,900
Come on, Ryo-san.

167
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:47,860
Yes.

168
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:53,360
By the way, Ryo-san,

169
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:55,240
I've actually got a favor to ask.

170
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:58,040
Why don't you just stay
in this house for good?

171
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,100
Well...

172
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:02,180
I mean it, Ryo-san.

173
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:06,100
We don't mind if you stay as long as you like,
you know.

174
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:08,140
Please do, big brother.

175
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,740
That's very kind of you, but...

176
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:12,380
As for me,

177
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:13,900
That's right.

178
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:17,360
That's it! Ryo-san,
why don't you become our adopted son?

179
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:19,520
Adopt?

180
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:23,340
If he'd just become Aya's husband,
that'd be nice.

181
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,842
Hey, Aya.
Ryo-san would be fine, wouldn't he?

182
00:11:27,892 --> 00:11:30,520
You don't mind him either, do you?

183
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:37,020
Dad, you idiot!

184
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:41,460
What's with him?

185
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:44,480
He really is an idiot, this guy.

186
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,820
What do you mean?

187
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:47,740
I'm calling him an idiot because he is one.

188
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:50,180
Stop calling people idiot, idiot, idiot.

189
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:57,800
It's been a month today, hasn't it.

190
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:01,320
Still no word from Ryo-chan?

191
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:02,340
Yes.

192
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:04,660
According to the people
at the shopping district,

193
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:07,860
the last time anyone saw him was when he left,
saying he'd go finagle some time off work.

194
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:10,100
That's the last sighting we have, though.

195
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:16,440
Without that guy around, no problems happen.
It's peaceful, and that's nice.

196
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,240
Chief...

197
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:18,780
What is it?

198
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:20,540
The file's upside down.

199
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,500
What's wrong, Terai?

200
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:27,360
That.

201
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:32,700
That person in the lower
left corner of this show?

202
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,440
Ryo-chan!

203
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:38,460
What? In Hakodate?

204
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:53,880
Goodbye.

205
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,860
Hey, miss.

206
00:12:59,580 --> 00:13:02,200
Wanna come hang out with us somewhere nice?

207
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,740
We're so bored, it's killing us.

208
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:06,320
Why don't you keep us company?

209
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:07,840
No, thanks.

210
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:10,320
Don't be so cold about it.

211
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:11,420
-Come on!-No!

212
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,100
Come on, quit it!

213
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:14,120
I said no!

214
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:16,900
Who's there!

215
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:19,480
Ryo-san!

216
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:21,240
Who the hell are you?

217
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,340
Don't get in our way!

218
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:26,140
That's cheap! Two grown men ganging up!

219
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:29,780
Shut up! Don't play the hero, you bastard!

220
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:31,200
Stand back!

221
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:34,520
I'll handle this!

222
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,280
Got him!

223
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:40,980
Little rich brat!

224
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:42,140
No way!

225
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,760
You're not hurt, are you?

226
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:45,620
I'm fine.

227
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,060
I see.

228
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:54,180
What's wrong?

229
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:57,800
I was scared.

230
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:14,820
Hey, Ryo-san.

231
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:17,840
Your memory still hasn't come back?

232
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:18,440
Yeah.

233
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,860
If your memory comes back,

234
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:23,400
When your memory comes back,

235
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:25,220
will you go away somewhere?

236
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:28,460
Big brother was saying,

237
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:31,700
thanks to you,
we might be able to buy a new boat.

238
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:35,820
He said he hopes you could keep
helping us like this forever.

239
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:39,820
Ryo-san...

240
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:43,300
Don't go anywhere.
Stay here with us forever!

241
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:44,360
Aya-chan...

242
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:46,400
Th-that is, I...

243
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:49,380
I... I really like you, Ryo-san...

244
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:56,680
Hey, Aya-chan!

245
00:14:57,980 --> 00:15:01,620
Hey, hey, go on ahead and head home.

246
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:02,220
Mm.

247
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:10,280
Mm, you went to visit Eperuzā

248
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:20,960
She was a beautiful woman. From what I could see,
she seemed like a wife who came looking for someone who'd gone missing.

249
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:27,200
See you.

250
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:32,180
Excuse me.

251
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:35,420
I'd like to ask you something.

252
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,860
I'm looking for this man.

253
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,120
Do you have any idea where he might be?

254
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:43,500
Who is this guy?

255
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:46,120
His name is Kankichi Ryotsu.

256
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:48,040
Is he your husband or something?

257
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,280
No, actually, I...

258
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:56,120
Did he do something?

259
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,160
Well, sort of.

260
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:00,380
So, does he look familiar at all?

261
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:03,000
No, I've never seen him.

262
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:03,800
I see.

263
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:33,100
Big bro

264
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:39,400
Big bro

265
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:39,620
That

266
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:42,120
Looks like it's mine.

267
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:46,280
Looks like I'm being hunted by the police.

268
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:51,240
If I stay here like this,

269
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:53,500
I'll only end up causing everyone trouble,

270
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:56,000
so I've decided to disappear from here.

271
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:57,160
Big bro

272
00:16:58,480 --> 00:17:01,380
The police are looking
for you at the harbor.

273
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:03,900
I see.

274
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:05,880
Run, big bro!

275
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:06,740
Ryoji

276
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:07,920
You

277
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:10,300
Whether the police are after you or not,

278
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,800
you're still my big bro.

279
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:13,160
Come on, hurry.

280
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,200
Ryo-san

281
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,140
You're really leaving

282
00:17:29,660 --> 00:17:30,540
See ya.

283
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:46,380
Ryo-chan

284
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,620
I finally found you.

285
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:52,280
Who are you?

286
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:55,300
Stop playing dumb already.

287
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:57,120
We've searched for you for so long.

288
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:59,280
Searched? For me?

289
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:00,220
That's right.

290
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:01,720
And as for you,

291
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,540
Big brother, don't let her fool you.

292
00:18:04,540 --> 00:18:05,800
This one's a cop.

293
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:06,740
A cop?

294
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,220
What are you talking about?

295
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:12,000
Come on, you're coming with me.

296
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:16,840
You're not getting past here.

297
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,320
Who the hell are you?

298
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:19,260
You startled me!

299
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:21,740
What are you doing?

300
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:22,620
Big brother, now's our chance!

301
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:24,800
Sorry, Ryotsu.

302
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:33,480
Whaaaat!

303
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,060
You're a reckless one

304
00:18:41,060 --> 00:18:43,920
What?

305
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:57,520
Kei-chan!

306
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:16,820
Senpai, please stop!

307
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:24,820
What are you -

308
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,760
Yes!

309
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:40,640
Senpai, why?

310
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:46,100
Boat ahead, stop your vessel!

311
00:19:49,780 --> 00:19:52,740
Ryo-chan, stop quietly and surrender.

312
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:25,140
What was I doing all this time...

313
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:25,820
Right.

314
00:20:26,900 --> 00:20:29,300
That was, if I remember right,
the shopkeepers

315
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:30,900
pressing me to pay my tab,

316
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:33,080
and I claimed I had a sure
way to get a big sum of money,

317
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,540
and I ended up boasting big.

318
00:20:35,460 --> 00:20:36,440
What's this?

319
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:39,060
This year, the crab catch is low,

320
00:20:39,060 --> 00:20:40,640
and the prices have been climbing.

321
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:43,980
If we catch crabs and sell them off,

322
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:46,220
If I could get a fortune quickly,

323
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:49,020
I chartered a fishing boat
and went out crab fishing.

324
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:50,500
Then we ran into a huge storm,

325
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:58,740
and I was thrown into the raging sea.

326
00:20:58,740 --> 00:21:00,960
When I came to, I was in that harbor town.

327
00:21:01,540 --> 00:21:01,860
Right.

328
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:03,920
Whatever happened,
I had to keep hold of my gun.

329
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,600
I never let go of it.

330
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:06,640
I see.

331
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:08,340
I remember everything!

332
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:09,620
That's good.

333
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:18,020
I gave it my all, but in the end we couldn't catch enough, so I can't pay the money back.
If the Chief finds out about this, we're in big trouble.

334
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:22,240
This is bad, really bad.
What am I going to do?

335
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,820
He's really gone, isn't he, Ryo-san?

336
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:40,380
Yeah.

337
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:48,000
Ryo-san has amnesia?

338
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,920
Yes. According to Reiko's report,
it seems that's the case.

339
00:21:52,620 --> 00:21:54,860
So that's why we haven't
heard from him for a month.

340
00:21:59,420 --> 00:22:00,740
I'm back.

341
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:02,760
Ryotsu!

342
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:03,760
Ryo-san!

343
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:07,520
Who are you?

344
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:10,100
Are you really suffering from amnesia?

345
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:12,240
Don't you recognize me?

346
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:16,380
Sorry, I can't remember.

347
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:20,200
You said you were going
to the crab dormitory,

348
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,520
and then you disappeared.

349
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:25,580
But an invoice for the fishing
boat fees has arrived at my place.

350
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:28,160
Do you really not remember?

351
00:22:29,580 --> 00:22:30,460
Well...

352
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:32,180
Ryotsu.

353
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:36,560
Sorry, I really can't remember at all.

354
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,740
I see.

355
00:22:37,740 --> 00:22:38,920
Ryo-san.

356
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:45,160
Apparently I've caused you
all tremendous trouble here.

357
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:49,280
I'll leave this town.

358
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:53,740
I don't want to cause
you all any more trouble.

359
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:56,460
Please just let me go.

360
00:22:57,500 --> 00:23:00,560
Wait, Ryotsu! It's no trouble at all.

361
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:03,860
You're someone this police box needs.

362
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:06,520
That's right, don't go, Ryo-san.

363
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:09,040
We'll miss you, Ryo-chan.

364
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:10,550
Senpai! We -

365
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:13,780
You all really care about me that much...

366
00:23:13,780 --> 00:23:14,720
Uuuu...

367
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:19,500
Then, may I stay here?

368
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:20,840
Of course you can.

369
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:23,620
Thank you, Chief.

370
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:26,480
Chief Ohara is so generous.

371
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:28,940
Chief Ohara.

372
00:23:28,940 --> 00:23:32,480
How do you know my name?

373
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:35,560
Why do I know that? I can't remember.

374
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:36,960
Up we go.

375
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:40,820
So the amnesia was all a lie from the start?

376
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:43,660
No, it was real at first.

377
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:54,160
I remembered, so I was right all along.
You bastard, I'll never forgive you!

378
00:23:54,820 --> 00:23:55,240
Hey.

379
00:23:56,620 --> 00:24:01,060
Ryo-chan, once your memory comes back,
it'll be this all over again...

380
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:11,280
Welcome, please come in.

381
00:24:12,620 --> 00:24:13,940
Welcome!

382
00:24:14,460 --> 00:24:16,000
Welcome, please come in.

383
00:24:17,340 --> 00:24:18,720
Welcome!

384
00:24:19,220 --> 00:24:20,620
Welcome!

385
00:24:21,620 --> 00:24:23,740
Um uh uh, so...

386
00:24:23,740 --> 00:24:25,240
Excuse me, is this okay?

387
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:26,100
Welcome!

388
00:24:26,100 --> 00:24:28,380
Then, a natto roll,
a salmon roll, and a sara roll.

389
00:24:28,380 --> 00:24:30,220
Anything rolls, rolls... what should I do?

390
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:31,640
Right.

391
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:34,180
Do you have California rolls?

392
00:24:34,180 --> 00:24:36,220
We don't have California rolls.

393
00:24:37,120 --> 00:24:38,840
This isn't America, you know.

394
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:40,460
Sorry, Sori.

395
00:24:40,460 --> 00:24:42,940
Well,

396
00:24:42,990 --> 00:24:45,160
Excuse me!

397
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,420
Yes, welcome!

398
00:24:46,950 --> 00:24:49,380
So, skewered fried foods,
mixed tempura fritters, pork cutlet,

399
00:24:49,430 --> 00:24:51,620
what was it, fried everything, fried...?

400
00:24:52,180 --> 00:24:53,580
What do you recommend?

401
00:24:54,740 --> 00:24:56,860
Just be careful with the pork cutlet.

402
00:24:58,200 --> 00:25:00,560
Was that a dad joke?

403
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:02,360
Yes, sorry, sorry.

404
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:04,680
I don't get it.

405
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:08,300
Ah? Hm? Huh? Eh? Huh? Eh?

406
00:25:08,420 --> 00:25:09,100
Seriously?

407
00:25:10,020 --> 00:25:13,100
Welcome, welcome, come on in.

408
00:25:13,740 --> 00:25:15,463
Welcome!

409
00:25:15,513 --> 00:25:17,820
Welcome, come on in.

410
00:25:18,520 --> 00:25:22,520
Welcome, welcome, come on in.

411
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:26,920
Welcome, welcome, good to see you.

412
00:25:29,580 --> 00:25:33,260
I was asked to look after the
Nishikigoi while the Chief was away.

413
00:25:33,260 --> 00:25:36,460
I thought it was an easy part-time job,
just feeding the koi,

414
00:25:36,460 --> 00:25:39,820
but Koichiro,
the Chief's favorite, ran away!

415
00:25:39,820 --> 00:25:41,700
Koichiro, come back!

416
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:43,840
Well, now there's only one way.

417
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:47,360
Next time: Nishikigoi Koi Panic,
see you then.

418
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:53,000
Thank you.

